---
import trace from '../../../../artifacts/functional-laptop/chapters/41-corpus-preparation/corpus-preparation-trace.json';
import InlineMath from '../InlineMath.astro';

const roles = [
  { key: 'train', name: 'Training', use: 'Learn tokenizer choices and fit the model.' },
  { key: 'validation', name: 'Validation', use: 'Select settings; do not learn tokenizer choices from this text.' },
  { key: 'test', name: 'Test', use: 'Reserve for final evaluation; do not fit the model or tokenizer on this text.' },
] as const;
---
<figure class="course-diagram corpus-preparation-diagram" data-diagram-style="course-v1"
  data-visualization-id="corpus-preparation" tabindex="0"
  aria-labelledby="corpus-preparation-title" aria-describedby="corpus-preparation-description">
  <figcaption class="course-diagram__caption">
    <h3 id="corpus-preparation-title">Prepare documents outside the Rust language model</h3>
    <p id="corpus-preparation-description" class="course-diagram__description">
      The six-document course fixture passes through NeMo's word-count rule and
      exact duplicate removal, leaving three documents. A fixed policy assigns
      known source groups to training, validation and test; Rust loads the exported
      records. Document counts count those records. Decoded text bytes measure only
      the UTF-8 size of their text, excluding metadata. Neither quantity certifies
      privacy, complete related-source discovery or trained-model quality.
    </p>
  </figcaption>
  <div class="course-diagram__grid preparation-flow">
    <section class="course-diagram__card-stack" data-diagram-card data-diagram-box>
      <h4>1. Declare the source and policy</h4>
      <p>Keep document IDs, source-group metadata and intended-use context. Freeze
        quality and split choices before observing their outcomes.</p>
      <dl>
        <dt>Fixture input documents</dt>
        <dd class="course-diagram__technical"><code>{trace.documents.input}</code></dd>
      </dl>
    </section>
    <section class="course-diagram__card-stack" data-diagram-card data-diagram-box>
      <h4>2. Run external NeMo preparation</h4>
      <dl>
        <dt>After the word-count rule</dt>
        <dd class="course-diagram__technical"><code>{trace.documents.after_quality}</code> document occurrences</dd>
        <dt>After exact duplicate removal</dt>
        <dd class="course-diagram__technical"><code>{trace.documents.prepared}</code> documents</dd>
        <dt>Final document-retention fraction</dt>
        <dd><InlineMath latex={'\\frac{' + trace.documents.prepared + '}{' + trace.documents.input + '}'} /></dd>
      </dl>
      <p>The fraction divides the final prepared count by the original input count
        of <code>{trace.documents.input}</code> documents.</p>
      <p>One cat-story occurrence remains. Either original cat-story ID may be kept.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="course-diagram__card-stack" data-diagram-card data-diagram-box>
      <h4>3. Export and load the selected role</h4>
      <p>NeMo-prepared JSONL crosses into a caller-supplied Rust reader. Loading
        validates records and limits, not their suitability for training.</p>
      <dl>
        <dt>All-role inspection export loaded by Rust</dt>
        <dd><code>{trace.loading.all_roles.documents}</code> documents;
          <code>{trace.loading.all_roles.text_utf8_bytes}</code> decoded text bytes</dd>
        <dt>Training export loaded by Rust</dt>
        <dd><code>{trace.loading.training_only.documents}</code> document;
          <code>{trace.loading.training_only.text_utf8_bytes}</code> decoded text bytes</dd>
      </dl>
    </section>
  </div>
  <section class="course-diagram__card-stack" data-diagram-card data-diagram-box>
    <h4>The provided groups keep the three learning roles separate</h4>
    <div class="course-diagram__grid preparation-role-grid">
      {roles.map(role => <section class="course-diagram__card-stack" data-diagram-card data-diagram-box data-corpus-role={role.key}>
        <h4>{role.name}</h4>
        <p><code>{trace.splits[role.key].documents}</code> fixture document;
          <code>{trace.splits[role.key].decoded_text_utf8_bytes}</code> decoded text bytes.</p>
        <p>{role.use}</p>
      </section>)}
    </div>
    <p class="course-diagram__description">Only the training export supplies
      tokenizer learning. Disjoint role labels alone do not prove that near-copies
      or protected benchmark text are absent.</p>
  </section>
</figure>

<style>
  .preparation-flow,
  .preparation-role-grid {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    align-items: start;
  }

  @container (min-width: 55rem) {
    .preparation-flow,
    .preparation-role-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
</style>
